A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report belongs with an open ticket when evidence establishes the **same cause**
([decision 0003](/kb/decisions/0003-signed-4471-review), replacing the unchanged
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):

1. read the report and look up its tenant, locale, booking-form version, and channel;
2. for the known date causes, evaluate `causeOf` and check `sameCause`;
3. merge only when the cause is established as the same; otherwise keep reports separate.

<Callout>
Matching subjects can hide different causes; different subjects can describe the same cause.
Intake tags and browser locale are not substitutes for the tenant directory.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate and request the missing evidence. An unknown tenant or unsupported
case must not be merged on subject alone. The date classifier covers the known parser and
hint problems, not every product handled by the desk.
